const faqs=[
 ['Can foreigners buy property in South Africa?','Yes. In general, non-residents can buy and own residential property in South Africa, either in their own name or through a structure such as a company or trust. Rules can differ for certain types of land, so we check what applies to the property you are considering.'],
 ['Can I get a mortgage as a non-resident?','Several South African banks offer home loans to non-residents, usually covering a portion of the purchase price, with the balance paid from funds brought in from abroad. Terms vary by bank and by your circumstances, and our financial partners can assess what is realistic for you.'],
 ['Do I need to be in South Africa to buy?','Not necessarily. Much of the process can be handled remotely, with documents signed abroad and certified where required. We coordinate each step so you know when, or whether, you need to travel.'],
 ['What does ESIE charge?','After the introductory call we send a personalised quote based only on the services you need, with a clear and transparent scope.'],
 ['What costs are there besides the purchase price?','Typically transfer duty, which is charged on a sliding scale, conveyancing and registration fees, and bond registration costs if you finance the purchase. We outline the expected costs early so there are no surprises.'],
 ['How do I bring money into South Africa?','Funds are transferred through an authorised dealer, usually a bank. Keeping the right records when money comes in makes it simpler to take proceeds out again in future. Our foreign exchange partners guide you through it.'],
 ['What tax will I pay as an owner?','It depends on how you use the property and where you are tax resident. Rental income, and capital gains when you sell, may be taxable in South Africa and possibly in your home country. Our tax partners explain what applies to you.'],
 ['Should I buy in my own name, a company or a trust?','Each option has different implications for tax, estate planning and administration. Our specialists help you choose the structure that suits your goals.'],
 ['How long does the process take?','Once an offer is accepted, transfer and registration commonly take a few months, depending on finance, documentation and the deeds office. We keep you updated at every stage.']
];
